{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"admapix","displayName":"AdMapix","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fly0pants/skills/admapix","publisherHandle":"fly0pants","publisherDisplayName":"fly0pants","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fly0pants","version":"1.0.30","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1781852959124,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/admapix/card?ownerHandle=fly0pants&version=1.0.30","sha256":"5cc9c1d13ff69fbb3d1372d19f1163663c5aee1ab223c026b33d54297a54a852","size":2965,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"334e0b600b7eebae4535f8ae514d0804cbb709731c06a4e0c5344f8bc1f5b087","bundleFingerprints":["d9b33513f56d5b7a3a888fa1ba6d206382a310a3a874f071a5837a0a89661624","04562a0dbba0d70a7eca9ed59ae0b2b9180210eb70a814a24a8a6bfdc4a0dddc"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":4933,"sha256":"1176868ec010cd80c87f6b99247d0b628f50a79e9d695a3d2ba0a5d698d6fbdf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README_CN.md","size":4712,"sha256":"ceb3dc52205cc2ce33278848db54d47d54055f23eb9670ffcc9c254f62186001","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8926,"sha256":"9ce5853320e0f538e71df19043d2b9ca38b14c3817b783503f27cccf80c8791b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-creative.md","size":14633,"sha256":"38a22e068715eb6d1247ba09fd726ee0c7cfeb19921eb6deb2a882583c9ed2d5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-download-revenue.md","size":4103,"sha256":"c72832090a05ce4545eec863adae2552390721011ac8159e066f8a9288985353","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-product.md","size":16268,"sha256":"d039edc5ef2a0615177e425a13fe0e889c00984c94c6302b08826fc4b3d5416a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-ranking.md","size":7822,"sha256":"9c26111dbc00063201fbefb6889fd57253be800362534d6864ca9b0fb3124c49","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-market.md","size":6082,"sha256":"178f1fe4ae1c36f4123a8b9143345d0077ca88ba12e69f89ee2fcd2a60db0bc3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/param-mappings.md","size":5593,"sha256":"a9732b5b378ef374f0c73f14a32d243a18f3f1dfad48cdbb036f0846062aca62","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-distribution.md","size":5409,"sha256":"92b1e91922cae5fdb251b79265884fe99742124d6951b9798d8ec745739f5767","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent AdMapix API client, but its install docs use an unpinned npx command that can execute mutable remote installer code.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789172185937,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Package Execution During Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"README.md"},"region":{"startLine":19,"endLine":23}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"8b5ccd9a5a5a75cd"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `README.md`, lines 19–23  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Supply-chain risk caused by unpinned package execution  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```markdown\n  ## Install\n\n  ```bash\n  npx clawhub install admapix\n  ```\n  ```\n\n  The same installation instruction is duplicated in `README_CN.md`, lines 19–23.\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The documented installation command invokes `clawhub` through `npx` without specifying a package version or integrity constraint. If the package is not already available in a trusted local cache, `npx` can retrieve the current package release from its configured registry and execute it with the installing user's permissions.\n\n  Because the resolved package may change after this Skill has been audited, the effective installation code is not reproducible or bounded to the reviewed repository contents. Registry-account compromise, a malicious future release, dependency compromise, or registry configuration manipulation could therefore introduce arbitrary executable behavior.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises the publisher account, package distribution channel, or a transitive dependency used by the unpinned `clawhub` release.\n  2. The attacker publishes a malicious version or causes dependency resolution to select malicious code.\n  3. A user follows the documented command:\n     `npx clawhub install admapix`.\n  4. `npx` resolves and downloads the attacker-controlled package version.\n  5. The package CLI or applicable lifecycle code executes under the user's account.\n  6. The malicious code can access resources available to that account, subject to operating-system and sandbox restrictions.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation could provide arbitrary code execution with the privileges of the user running the installation command. Potential scope includes reading or modifying user-accessible files, accessing environment variables and locally available credentials, installing altered Skill content, and initiating outbound network connections.\n\n  This finding does not establish that the current `clawhub` package is malicious. It identifies an unsafe, mutable dependency-execution pattern in the installation documentation.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin `clawhub` to a specifically reviewed version:\n     ```bash\n     npx clawhub@&lt;verified-version&gt; install admapix\n     ```\n  2. Use an exact version rather than a floating tag or range.\n  3. Document the expected package registry and publisher identity.\n  4. Where supported, verify package provenance, signatures, and integrity hashes before execution.\n  5. Review and lock transitive dependencies associated with the selected installer version.\n  6. Apply the same corrected command to `README_CN.md`.\n  7. Prefer an installation workflow that separates package download and verification from execution."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789172082.4999714,"endTime":1789172139.09202}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"admapix","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v574r8sm2bdwxjfhxpavpj3nc58e7k9f-iPPbMv/clawscan-skillspector-1652693610/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T00:14:41.515605+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":86,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":81,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4933,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"README_CN.md","type":"markdown","lines":81,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4712,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":164,"executable":false,"size_bytes":8926,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-creative.md","type":"markdown","lines":477,"executable":false,"size_bytes":14633,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-distribution.md","type":"markdown","lines":182,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5409,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-download-revenue.md","type":"markdown","lines":187,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4103,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-market.md","type":"markdown","lines":178,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6082,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-product.md","type":"markdown","lines":550,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16268,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-ranking.md","type":"markdown","lines":237,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7822,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/param-mappings.md","type":"markdown","lines":127,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5593,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"P6","finding_id":"finding-27a821dec59c43a4a5ddd6cda308972d","category":"System Prompt Leakage","pattern":"Direct Prompt Extraction","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":142,"end_line":null},"finding":"Output Rules","explanation":"Skill contains instructions that could directly expose system prompts, internal rules, or hidden instructions to users or external parties.","remediation":"Remove any instructions that reveal, print, or output system prompts or internal rules. System instructions should never be exposed to end users.","code_snippet":"\nFor the creative `search` endpoint, `page_size` is capped at **10** (clamp any larger request down to 10; use `page` for more). Other list endpoints use their own documented ranges.\n\n## Output Rules\n\nReturn the API response as **raw structured JSON** — keep the API field names; do not rename, drop, summarize, rank, or editorialize. The calling agent composes and analyzes.\n","intent":null,"tags":["System Prompt Leakage","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4c935f6a60234a527cd7ec0e4a1671bbaeb6d29720d4470bac5369da008a8085","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":142,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-66f9d74bfcc54d1ea3fcd426a4611e58","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README instructs users to run `npx clawhub install admapix` without pinning a specific version. This causes execution of whatever package version is current at install time, which creates a supply-chain risk if the package is later compromised, typo-squatted, or updated with malicious postinstall/runtime behavior. In a skill-install context, that risk is meaningful because users are being told to execute remote code directly from a package registry.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and version users should execute, and preferably document integrity-verifiable installation steps. For example, instruct users to use a fixed version (`npx clawhub@<version> install admapix` if supported), publish checksums/signatures or immutable release references, and recommend reviewing release notes before upgrading.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7262d2d74474470a7918d81d46269adc58e41b14f04615fa861813226ce136df","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-8a035569e75b49f49d1442cd5941df55","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README instructs users to run `npx clawhub install admapix` without pinning a specific package version. This can cause users to execute whatever version is currently published or resolved at install time, which creates a supply-chain risk if the package is updated maliciously, compromised, or changed incompatibly.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and/or tool version in installation instructions, for example by specifying an immutable version. Prefer documented installation flows that verify package provenance, use lockfiles where applicable, and reference trusted release artifacts or checksums.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7262d2d74474470a7918d81d46269adc58e41b14f04615fa861813226ce136df","occurrences":[{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ff8a685b5a5c4383a0b03fc5833dcc51","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description includes very broad triggers such as ad creative, rankings, downloads, revenue, and market data without strong activation constraints. This can cause over-invocation and unintended routing of user requests to this skill, increasing the chance that user queries and derived parameters are sent to an external API when the user did not clearly intend that action.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger description to explicit use cases and require clearer activation criteria, such as only invoking for requests that explicitly ask for AdMapix data or ad intelligence lookups. Add gating language that the skill should be used only when external API access is necessary and user intent is clear.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-e3f2799fe83a4dfbb28221297471330f","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}?{params}\" -H \"$admapix_auth_header\"\n# POST\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}\" \\\n  -H \"$admapix_auth_header\" -H \"Content-","explanation":"The skill explicitly sends user-derived query parameters and an API credential to an external service at api.admapix.com. Even though this is the intended function of the skill, it still creates a real data egress boundary where sensitive prompts, search terms, or business intelligence queries could be transmitted to a third party.","remediation":"Document and enforce strict data minimization before requests are made, and require explicit user intent for external lookups. Validate and constrain which user inputs can be forwarded, redact unnecessary sensitive fields, and add clear consent and auditing around third-party transmission.","code_snippet":"```bash\nadmapix_auth_header=\"X-API-Key: ${ADMAPIX_API_KEY}\"\n# GET\ncurl -s \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}?{params}\" -H \"$admapix_auth_header\"\n# POST\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}\" \\\n  -H \"$admapix_auth_header\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{...}'","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6d1724b8d3c0faeb2b558f935ae1a52820292a5be21d91961012eace21815ef3","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-8bc025b27d1945348ed9f2ba3ae46935","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.admapix.com/","explanation":"The skill explicitly sends user-derived query parameters and an API credential to an external service at api.admapix.com. Even though this is the intended function of the skill, it still creates a real data egress boundary where sensitive prompts, search terms, or business intelligence queries could be transmitted to a third party.","remediation":"Document and enforce strict data minimization before requests are made, and require explicit user intent for external lookups. Validate and constrain which user inputs can be forwarded, redact unnecessary sensitive fields, and add clear consent and auditing around third-party transmission.","code_snippet":"```bash\nadmapix_auth_header=\"X-API-Key: ${ADMAPIX_API_KEY}\"\n# GET\ncurl -s \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}?{params}\" -H \"$admapix_auth_header\"\n# POST\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}\" \\\n  -H \"$admapix_auth_header\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{...}'","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d5aede409ddd8a138e88adad8a13d1f2e85d4c70e4b3b7759eb0a00fae3b81d7","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-9cb986b0662f49e08871b67f3f63a76f","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.admapix.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"# GET\ncurl -s \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}?{params}\" -H \"$admapix_auth_header\"\n# POST\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.admapix.com/api/data/{endpoint}\" \\\n  -H \"$admapix_auth_header\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{...}'\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d5aede409ddd8a138e88adad8a13d1f2e85d4c70e4b3b7759eb0a00fae3b81d7","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-183630e59bba49b6b65d4a50d97a27a6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":123,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"      \"playHtmlFp\": [],\n      \"playHtmlUrl\": [],\n      \"demoadCnt\": 1,\n      \"appList\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"6498883328\",\n          \"cnt\": null,","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":123,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-183630e59bba49b6b65d4a50d97a27a6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":140,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"      \"playHtmlFp\": [],\n      \"playHtmlUrl\": [],\n      \"demoadCnt\": 1,\n      \"appList\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"6498883328\",\n          \"cnt\": null,","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":140,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-183630e59bba49b6b65d4a50d97a27a6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":192,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"      \"playHtmlFp\": [],\n      \"playHtmlUrl\": [],\n      \"demoadCnt\": 1,\n      \"appList\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"6498883328\",\n          \"cnt\": null,","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":192,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-183630e59bba49b6b65d4a50d97a27a6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":194,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"      \"playHtmlFp\": [],\n      \"playHtmlUrl\": [],\n      \"demoadCnt\": 1,\n      \"appList\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"6498883328\",\n          \"cnt\": null,","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":194,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-183630e59bba49b6b65d4a50d97a27a6","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":195,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"      \"playHtmlFp\": [],\n      \"playHtmlUrl\": [],\n      \"demoadCnt\": 1,\n      \"appList\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"6498883328\",\n          \"cnt\": null,","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":195,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-bfd881f446e74b819dc9b629db3301af","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":178,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"The documentation explicitly notes that appList[].name may contain HTML tags and instructs consumers to strip them before display. If a caller fails to sanitize or safely encode this field, untrusted HTML from the upstream API could be rendered in downstream web/chat surfaces, creating an injection/XSS risk.","remediation":"Treat all upstream string fields as untrusted. Update the skill docs to require output encoding/sanitization before rendering, prefer plain-text rendering, and explicitly forbid passing API-provided HTML through to web views or rich-message templates without a vetted sanitizer.","code_snippet":"\n### ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n1. **HTML tags in names:** `appList[].name` may contain HTML highlight tags like `<font color='red'>keyword</font>`. Strip these before displaying to the user.\n2. **Null values:** Many fields can be `null` — always handle null gracefully.\n3. **totalSize null:** For keyword searches, `totalSize` is often `null`. The actual result count is reflected in `list` length per page.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":178,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-684b395f50d148409d2099c3f720999b","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":193,"end_line":null},"finding":"pList","explanation":"This line documents list[].appList[].name and explicitly warns it may contain HTML font tags. In this skill context, which returns raw JSON for downstream composition, that makes the data-flow risk more relevant: a consuming agent/UI might directly render this field, enabling markup/script injection if sanitization is missed.","remediation":"Document that appList[].name must be HTML-decoded/stripped and contextually escaped before any display. Prefer returning a separate sanitized plain-text field or sanitizing within the skill before exposing the data to downstream components.","code_snippet":"| list[].title | Ad title (may be null) |\n| list[].describe | Ad copy text (may be null) |\n| list[].appList[].name | Associated app name — **may contain HTML `<font>` tags** |\n| list[].appList[].developer | Developer/publisher name |\n| list[].appList[].developerId | Developer ID |\n| list[].appList[].logo | App icon URL |\n| list[].impression | Estimated impression count |","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db6e0668ac096eab548e407e69bf059ebea51006d56c3468d4c6245ee5980ba5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-creative.md","start_line":193,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-731df55f40754e41ab3d8caa13a5d4d3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":58,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"The 